On Consensus — Dual License
===========================

This repository is dual-licensed. The split mirrors the editorial decision
that the prose is a creative-commons publication and the build chassis
underneath it is free software.

1.  **Editorial content** — every Markdown / HTML article, the prose inside
    layouts and includes, all author bios, series notes, editorial pages,
    images under `images/`, and the prose copy in `_data/` — is licensed
    under the **Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
    License (CC BY-SA 4.0)**. See `LICENSE-CONTENT` for the full text.

2.  **Code, configuration, and stylesheets** — the Liquid templates'
    structural markup, every `.scss`, `.js`, `.yml`, and `.rb` file, the
    GitHub Actions workflows under `.github/workflows/`, the Decap CMS
    configuration under `admin/`, and the Jekyll build chassis itself — is
    licensed under the **MIT License**. See `LICENSE-CODE` for the full
    text.

When a single file mixes prose and code (a layout that contains structural
HTML and editorial copy, for example), the prose portion is CC BY-SA 4.0
and the structural portion is MIT. Reuse either under the terms that
match the part you are reusing.

The On Consensus name, masthead, and logo are not licensed for reuse and
remain the property of the publication.

Copyright © 2026 On Consensus and contributors.
